# Agent working files. The skills under .claude/ and .codex/ come from
# create-plugin and are committed; these do not. `settings.json` is a
# machine-local permission allowlist, and worktrees are whole checkouts —
# previously excluded only via .git/info/exclude, which no clone inherits.
/.claude/settings.json
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/worktrees/

# Internal design notes kept out of the published repository.
/internal-docs/

# Documentation site. Its build output is already covered by the `dist/` rule
# above; the cache is not, and it is large.
/docs/site/.vitepress/cache/

# Artefacts of the `validate-plugin` skill in `.config/`. It runs the validator
# through `npx --cache .cache/npm`, which parks npm's whole cache — hundreds of
# megabytes — in the repository root, alongside the archive it validates.
/.cache/
/ubica-keplergl-panel-*.zip

# Scratch of the subagent-driven-development skill: ledger, task briefs,
# implementer reports and review packages. Regenerable, and none of it belongs
# in a repository that is about to be published.
/.superpowers/

# The two per-country series the fire-emissions dashboard needs, derived from
# CAMS's own published data by testdata/make-firedata.py. Everything else that
# dashboard draws is read live from ECMWF; these exist only because DuckDB
# cannot read gzipped Arrow IPC over HTTP, and they regenerate in a minute.
#
# This rule is load-bearing rather than tidy. An earlier copy of these files was
# committed and had to be removed from every commit with git-filter-repo before
# the repository could go public — 61 MB in four blobs. Without the rule a
# single run of the recipe puts them back, untracked and easy to `git add -A`.
testdata/fire/
